A||||10||Tweek||Help! How do I get into my trunk/engine compartment?||||1||
Z||000000||Tweek||03-07-2001||04:24 PM||||Ok for some reason when I put the key in it dont turn, just as if it is the wrong key... Which kinda sucks cause about a mile from home today all of the sudden the voltage dropped to about 11. Which it does occasionaly when the belt gets real loose. So im pretty much stuck untill I can get in there to fix it... if need be I'll remove the lock and replace it later. I just dont know if that is possible..<P>Thanks for any help!!<P>-Ted<BR>'84 auto||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||03-07-2001||05:05 PM||||You don't have an SE do you? Too bad, They came with the electric trunk pop. You will have to drill out the lock. Try some WD-40 in it first before you break it. It may free up. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChopTop||03-07-2001||05:22 PM||||Possible some moisture got inside the lock and it's frozen up.  You can try dumping warm water on, or possible heating your key and then inserting it into the lock.  I've used the warm water method, but then you have to make sure you dry it off good later, otherwise it will just make it worse later.||||reg||1
Z||000003||c m west||03-07-2001||06:11 PM||||Yup, you will absolutley have to drill out the lock, once I got lucky with a coat hanger when I locked my keys in the trunk ( no open switch ), it may be possiblw to do this if you have enough patience<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jake_Dragon||03-07-2001||06:19 PM||||Imagine if you will you are closing your trunk lid and as it latches you hear your keys falling inside.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> That’s when my car got the name @#$%!@#@!!! I used a small screwdriver and was able to break the lock and get in.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">   <BR> <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/rebel33/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||03-07-2001||07:07 PM||||Only thing worse, would be to hear that jangling just as the lid locked - and the keys are on a chain inextricably hooked to your pants!  There you stand, chained to your car.<P>Nope - this never happened to anyone (I hope  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)- !  Just a funny scene popped into my head. ||||reg||10
Z||000006||Tweek||03-07-2001||09:19 PM||||Well, that was odd... I went out all ready to bust it open and I treid the key one more time, well, I think it knew I meant business cause it just opened right up... Thanks anyways! At least now I know what to do if it happens again and doesnt fix itself.<P>-Ted||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||03-07-2001||10:16 PM||||since you just got all the nasty weather in Maine, ill bet there is some moisture that froze, spray some WD40 or deicer in it so it wont do it again for a while. That one nice thing about remote door/trunk locks...let the ice come.||||reg||1
Z||000008||onfire||03-08-2001||03:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>since you just got all the nasty weather in Maine, ill bet there is some moisture that froze, spray some WD40 or deicer in it so it wont do it again for a while. That one nice thing about remote door/trunk locks...let the ice come.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, but what do you do when the battery dies and you lock your keys in the trunk?<P>||||reg||5
Z||000009||rogergarrison||03-08-2001||12:54 PM||||true, would only help if its froze. DONT lock your keys in trunk, lol. Hint, I always have an extra door key hidden.||||reg||1
